# live-pipeline
- label: a run↔session link is persisted in the run window's tq_session + tq_session_attr tmux user options via linkRunSession with a four-tier contract — attr "sid" (spawn identity: the run's own tq_session_id named the recording) and attr "pid" (pid-confirmed identity) are sticky forever, winning every poll and serve restart without re-resolution; attr "prompt" (content identity: the recording's first user message IS this run's persisted tq_prompt and no other party's) is served, settled for rivalry purposes (bars the path from other runs, stops contesting), and RE-VALIDATED every poll while the run lives — dropped to pending when a same-prompt rival whose gate admits the file makes content identity ambiguous, final on an exited run; attr "heur" (a guess — the sole eligible candidate, a unique prompt match under a coarse stone, or a resumed run's fresh source recording) is served but RE-VALIDATED on every poll — upgraded to pid/prompt when stronger evidence appears, dropped (cleared from tmux) the moment it turns out foreign, claimed, or contested, DEMOTED to pending the moment a second eligible candidate exists, and final on an exited run only when it was unambiguous at death (fact clha); nothing is persisted while pending, a failed persist still answers the link, and a link that would bind another run's recording is never persisted — tmux stays the only run table; src/mux/tmux.js exports setWindowOption plus setSessionOption/getSessionOption for session-scoped state, RUN_OPTION_NAMES includes tq_session_id + tq_ended + tq_resumed_path + tq_fork_prompt, and listWindows reports pane_pid + tq_session_attr + tq_session_id + tq_ended in its space-safe format and tq_session/tq_prompt/tq_resumed_path/tq_fork_prompt through id-keyed queries whose arbitrary-content value is placed last (locale-proof like window_name)
  id: clpr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'linkRunSession|spawn identity|run session link survives a serve restart' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: watching a run through /api/runs/session is LIVE and incremental: every poll re-links and re-stats the recording so events the agent appends appear in the next poll (integration: a stub agent writing claude-format JSONL grows 2→4 events, a second chapter opens, the mtimeMs-size etag moves); a request repeating the current etag answers {unchanged:true} with no session body, and the parse itself is memoized per path behind the etag so ~1s polls of an idle run cost one stat, never a reparse
  id: clfr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run session serves the growing unified session' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: run+session lifecycle is fully observable for the chat UI: GET /api/runs lists every run with sessionPath/link/attribution/state alongside the existing fields (state is pending|live|idle|exited — live only while generating), a run whose agent has not (or never will have) written a recording answers the pending shape (200, link pending, null session — never an error), a linked idle TUI answers state idle, an exited run's session stays served with state exited and the full final conversation, and a serve restarted mid-run answers the same linked session immediately from persisted tmux state
  id: clst
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run session of an exited run stays served|run session rejects malformed and unknown ids and answers pending|run session link survives a serve restart|GET /api/runs stays a plain GET route' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: run↔session attribution can never bind another agent's — or the user's — transcript to a run, even for agents that NEVER hold their recording open (the real claude behavior, and the round-2 failure mode): the integration stubs model it faithfully (recordings named by the spawn-assigned --session-id uuid, written open/append/close, lsof verifies ZERO holders at link time), and end-to-end against a real serve + tmux (a) two concurrent non-holding runs in ONE cwd with a sub-2s stagger BOTH link their own uuid recording as attribution sid — at no poll does either answer the other's transcript, and neither deadlocks pending-forever; (b) a user's own session file born after a run's start in the same cwd is NEVER served for that run — the run honestly pends until ITS uuid recording appears, then links it; (c) a poisoned pre-upgrade heuristic claim (the user's session persisted as tq_session attr heur) is dropped and CLEARED on the first poll after a serve restart instead of being served forever; the persisted tmux state carries attr sid so the correct links survive restarts
  id: clid
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'pid attribution|NON-HOLDING|NEVER served|poisoned pre-upgrade|spawn identity' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: run↔session attribution has a CONTENT-identity tier for the five registry agents WITHOUT a --session-id mechanism (codex, cursor-agent, opencode, droid, gemini): every prompted launch persists its prompt in the tq_prompt window option (activitySnippet single line), the linker extracts a candidate recording's FIRST user message (peekSession in the agent's own dialect, memoized per path — immutable once non-null), and promptCorroborates compares them (whitespace-collapsed; clipped 140-char prompts match by prefix, unclipped EXACTLY) so that (a) a candidate whose first message matches a DIFFERENT run's prompt — live, exited, or tombstoned, gated by that party's ownable time window — is FOREIGN and can never link here, (b) a candidate matching THIS run's prompt and nobody else's is CORROBORATED and links even while contested (attr prompt) — two prompted non-identity runs in ONE cwd disambiguate and serve their own transcripts while BOTH live, (c) identical prompts prove nothing: both runs stay pending (pending beats wrong), (d) self-recognition: a prompted run never links a recording whose known first message mismatches its own prompt, even uncontested with no rival in sight (the launder is refused even without a tombstone), (e) a rival whose prompt provably mismatches a recording's first message cannot contest it, so a bare run's own file stays linkable next to a prompted rival, and (f) a RESUMED run's follow-up tq_prompt is never content identity in either direction — a fork recording opens with the SOURCE conversation, not the follow-up prompt, so contentPromptOf substitutes tq_fork_prompt (fact clrs) and the follow-up never disowns or fakes ambiguity against anyone
  id: clpc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'prompt corroboration|prompt corroborates|two live prompted|identical prompts|mismatches its own prompt|NO user message|bare run|CAN.T own|disambiguates' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a dismissed run's claim on its recording OUTLIVES its tmux window (the r3 kill-launder fix): POST /api/runs/kill records a tombstone via recordRunTombstone BEFORE kill-window — {id, agent, cwd, started, killed, prompt, sessionId, session, attr} appended to the tq_tombstones SESSION-level tmux user option (base64 UTF-8 JSON: locale-proof ASCII, never tmux-format-expandable; RELEVANCE-capped at TOMBSTONE_MAX=32 — fact clrv — same-window entries replaced) — and readRunTombstones feeds every linkRunSession call (route handlers read once per request), so: a tombstone's claimed session path is excluded from every survivor's candidate set WHATEVER its attr, a tombstone that died PENDING keeps CONTESTING candidates born within its lifetime [started−2s, killed+2s] and keeps marking prompt-matching candidates foreign, while a tombstone that died WITH a claim bars only that path (a dead run never re-links, so it could never have owned anything else — no contested-forever), later-born files are never contested (a dead process writes nothing), a tombstone whose window still lives is ignored, garbage/absent state degrades to [], and tombstones survive serve restarts because they live in tmux — the end-to-end r3 scenario (slow-alpha survivor + killed fast-beta rival, prompted or bare) shows the survivor NEVER serving the dismissed run's transcript, before or after a restart, and linking its OWN recording when it appears
  id: cltb
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'tombstone|kill-launder|BARE survivor|kill tombstones|failed tombstone' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: tombstone RETENTION is by relevance, never recency (compactTombstones — the r4 contest-memory fix): a routine-dismissal flood can never evict the stone keeping an older contest honest — a stone is dropped ONLY when provably inert (no unsettled run window of its agent+cwd rivalry space — pending, heur- or prompt-linked, live or dead-pending; sid/pid links and dead runs' final claims are settled — has a candidate gate overlapping the stone's lifetime plus slack), same-space claimless stones with the same prompt MERGE into one interval-union entry (absorbed window ids remembered in ids[] so the ledger never double-tombstones them), and cap overflow FOLDS the oldest-killed stones into a COARSE per-space stone (interval-only, prompt unknown) instead of forgetting them — a coarse stone CONTESTS every candidate born inside its window and DEGRADES prompt corroboration there to guess-grade (the r5 secondary fix: a candidate whose first message uniquely matches THIS run's prompt and no known rival's SERVES under a promptUnknown owner, but only as re-validated attr heur, never settled attr prompt — an equal-prompt collider, e.g. a laundering run's own recording appearing with the same first message, demotes it again, and a bare candidate with no content match stays fully contested), while stones whose prompt matches a live unsettled run's content prompt are NEVER folded to coarse (fold the same-prompt twin's stone away and its recording would soft-corroborate as the survivor's own — same-prompt floods MERGE, so protection cannot blow the cap), so laundering stays non-final at any flood size; stones whose window still lives are kept verbatim and never merged; without a window list compaction degrades to the plain newest-N cap; end-to-end, 40 pure-API create+kill dismissal cycles after an identically-prompted twin's dismissal leave the survivor honest-pending at every poll — never serving the twin's transcript, before or after the flood — while its own late-born recording still links attr prompt
  id: clrv
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'r4 regression|routine same-space dismissals|COARSE stone|no unsettled run|window still LIVES|r4 vector 1' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: a run window that vanishes WITHOUT passing through POST /api/runs/kill (tmux kill-window / the default prefix-& binding / kill-session — even while serve is DOWN) still leaves a tombstone: run polls (GET /api/runs, GET /api/runs/session, and run resolution inside /api/sessions/live) reconcile the tq_run_ledger SESSION-level tmux option (base64 JSON of every live run window's id/agent/cwd/started/content-prompt/sessionId/claim+attr, written by syncRunLedger only when it changed, entered at run creation so a kill before the first poll is covered too, resumed runs ledgered with a BLANK content prompt) against the actual window list — a ledger entry whose window is GONE and whose id no tombstone answers for (merged ids[] included) gets a SYNTHESIZED tombstone carrying its last-known claim, prompt and lifetime with killed = the entry's stamped exit boundary (ended, for windows that died before vanishing) or detection time (at/after the real death, so the contested window only widens: pending beats wrong); API-killed runs are never double-tombstoned, the ledger survives serve restarts (tmux stays the only run table), and callers that stub the tmux layer must opt in via deps.syncRunLedger (stubbed windows are never synced into a real tmux server); end-to-end: a bare survivor NEVER serves a tmux-killed rival's transcript — the dead run's recording sits unserved beside the survivor's own — even when the kill-window happens while serve is stopped and the diff is only seen after a restart
  id: cllg
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run ledger|ledgered|synthesized|reconcile the ledger|r4 vector 2' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: prompt equality is corroboration, NOT identity (the r4 equal-prompt collision fix) — when the SAME first user message exists in two or more candidate recordings (e.g. the user's own session opens with the exact text the run was launched with), content identity selects nothing — attributeRunSession refuses to corroborate ANY collider, none of them may be served as a heuristic guess either, a persisted attr-prompt claim on one collider is dropped AND cleared from tmux the moment the second appears (the wrong transcript is never kept after the run's real recording lands), and the run stays honest-pending until another tier disambiguates (pid identity picks the recording the run's own tree holds) or a collider disappears (unique corroboration returns and the run links its own recording attr prompt)
  id: clqc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'equal-prompt|r4 vector 3' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
- label: the heuristic tier obeys the equal-prompt rule (the r5 promptless-mislink fix) — a guess needs a SOLE eligible candidate and dies with ambiguity, across the whole lifecycle: (a) selection — attributeRunSession answers no heuristic when two or more unvouched candidates survive the gate (birth order and anonymous fd holders are not identity), so a promptless run beside ANY concurrent same-space recording (incl. codex/droid machine-wide dated-tree spaces) stays honest-pending; (b) demotion — a persisted attr-heur guess is dropped AND cleared from tmux the moment a second eligible candidate exists (the user's session guessed during agent startup is demoted the moment the run's OWN recording lands — the wrong transcript is never kept), and relinks only when the candidate space collapses back to one (a collider claimed elsewhere, turned foreign, or gone); (c) exit boundary — the first poll that observes a run's death stamps tq_ended (detection time, at/after the real death; frozen once stamped, persisted in tmux), a dead run's candidate space is bounded to [tq_started−2s, tq_ended+2s], a guess that was UNIQUE for that whole window is the final answer forever (a later-born candidate can neither link nor demote it), and a guess that was AMBIGUOUS inside it is never finalized — cleared and pending, even when the ambiguity is first seen after the exit or across a serve restart; end-to-end (real serve + tmux + non-holding cursor-agent stub): promptless run + user session written in-cwd during startup → the sole-candidate guess serves transiently, is demoted to pending when the run's own recording appears, stays pending at every subsequent poll, and the exited run remains pending — the user's private chat is never the final answer; a BARE guess additionally serves a probation before it is served or finalized at all (fact clgp)
  id: clha
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'r5 vector|r5 regression|ambiguity rule|AMBIGUOUS at death|exit boundary|unambiguous at death|promptless codex' test/bin/tracequest-launch-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-live, implemented]
